1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,617
The average local business misses about forty percent of its incoming calls.

2
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:08,817
And every missed call is a customer who books with someone else.

3
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:13,017
Today we're going deep on the number one hustle from last week's video.

4
00:00:13,067 --> 00:00:15,483
AI automation for local businesses.

5
00:00:15,533 --> 00:00:18,750
The exact service, the tools, the pricing,

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:23,583
and how to land your first client. Let's get into it.

7
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:29,050
First, what are you actually selling? It's simple. An AI receptionist.

8
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,817
When a call gets missed,

9
00:00:30,867 --> 00:00:34,050
your system instantly texts the caller back.

10
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,383
An AI agent answers their questions,

11
00:00:36,433 --> 00:00:39,283
and books them straight into the calendar.

12
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:42,283
The owner does nothing. That's the magic.

13
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,383
You're not selling software.

14
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:47,250
You're selling recovered revenue.

15
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,617
Here's the stack, and you don't need to write code.

16
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:53,750
Make, or n8n, for the automation.

17
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,917
Twilio for the phone number and texting.

18
00:00:56,967 --> 00:00:59,917
An AI model behind it for the conversation.

19
00:00:59,967 --> 00:01:04,083
And Google Calendar, or the business's booking tool, on the end.

20
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:08,517
All together, that's about fifty dollars a month in running costs.

21
00:01:08,567 --> 00:01:10,217
Remember that number,

22
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:13,383
because the margins here are beautiful.

23
00:01:13,433 --> 00:01:16,050
The build itself has four steps.

24
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,217
One. A missed call triggers a webhook.

25
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:22,850
Two. The system sends an instant text.

26
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:26,717
Something like, sorry we missed you, how can we help?

27
00:01:26,767 --> 00:01:29,950
Three. The AI handles the conversation.

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,183
It knows the hours, the services, and the prices,

29
00:01:33,233 --> 00:01:36,083
because you gave it one simple document.

30
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:41,017
Four. It drops the booking into the calendar, and notifies the owner.

31
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:42,383
Build it once,

32
00:01:42,433 --> 00:01:46,917
and you can clone it for every new client in an afternoon.

33
00:01:46,967 --> 00:01:50,083
Now the pricing. Charge a setup fee.

34
00:01:50,133 --> 00:01:54,983
Five hundred to fifteen hundred dollars, depending on complexity.

35
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:56,917
Then a monthly retainer.

36
00:01:56,967 --> 00:02:02,217
Two hundred to five hundred a month, for hosting, monitoring and tweaks.

37
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:03,883
Do the math with me.

38
00:02:03,933 --> 00:02:08,150
If one recovered customer is worth three hundred dollars to a dentist,

39
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:12,483
your system only has to save one booking a month to pay for itself.

40
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:16,450
That's the pitch. And it sells itself.

41
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:19,250
So how do you get client number one?

42
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:21,450
Pick one niche in one city.

43
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,750
Dentists. Plumbers. Salons.

44
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,750
Then make an offer that's impossible to ignore.

45
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,650
A free two week pilot.

46
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:33,650
You set everything up, and you track every recovered call.

47
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,783
At the end, you show them one simple report.

48
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:41,083
We caught twelve missed calls, and booked five appointments.

49
00:02:41,133 --> 00:02:44,950
Then you ask for the monthly retainer, and for one referral.

50
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,983
Do that three times, and you have a real business.

51
00:02:49,033 --> 00:02:50,683
Now the honest part.

52
00:02:50,733 --> 00:02:54,317
Clients will churn, so keep onboarding new ones.

53
00:02:54,367 --> 00:02:58,850
You'll get support texts at weird hours, so set clear boundaries.

54
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,950
And don't oversell the AI.

55
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,283
It handles the routine eighty percent,

56
00:03:03,333 --> 00:03:05,750
and hands the rest to a human.

57
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:08,350
Under promise. Over deliver.

58
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:11,650
That's how you keep a retainer for years.

59
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:13,750
Here's your ninety day plan.

60
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:18,083
Month one. Build the system, and run one free pilot.

61
